  "plain_text": "Using Balena Etcher\nBalena Etcher is a convenient cross-platform program for writing ISO images to USB drives. Suitable for Windows, macOS, and Linux.\nImportant\nWarning: Incorrect device selection will result in data loss! Always double-check the selected drive and backup important data.\nDrive Requirements\nDrive Size\nSee Hardware Compatibility Guide for detailed system requirements and drive sizes.\nPreparation\nDownload Balena Etcher from the official website\nInstall the program on your OS\nConnect the USB drive\nCreating Bootable USB Drive\nLaunch Balena Etcher\nSelect the MiniOS ISO image:\nClick \"Flash from file\"\nSpecify the path to the ISO file\nSelect the target USB drive:\nClick \"Select target\"\nCheck the device model and size\nStart writing:\nClick \"Flash!\"\nWait for the process to complete (5–15 minutes)\nResult and persistence\nEtcher performs a raw image write: it copies the ISO layout to the whole target device. It does not create an ext4 partition in unused space, create a persistence session, or perform a MiniOS Installer deployment.\nPersistence is enabled only when a boot entry or kernel command line requests it, and it still requires suitable writable storage. See Boot modes and Initrd persistence before relying on saved changes.",
  "product_kind": "minios-markup-document",
  "schema_version": 1
}
